rl":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jappyjan","id":10154260,"login":"jappyjan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTU0MjYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/2c9f39cded109f19bdc09ccf8b75ed31b2babb02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:11:45Z","email":"jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jan Jaap"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:11:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wago): replace resource diagnostics dump with a focused warning card (#1899)\n\nThe WAGO section on the resource overview dumped raw text, listed every\nnode twice and embedded the full controller diagnostics panel.\n\n- Render nothing when the WAGO setup is healthy or the lookup fails.\n- Otherwise show a single HeroUI warning Alert: controller link, one line\n  per affected node (flow editor link) and the concrete conflicting\n  resources, linked.\n- Backend: stop duplicating this resource''s own nodes via the conflict\n  lookup and return conflicting resource ids/names.\n- Drop the dead jest ResourceDiagnostics.spec.tsx (no runner matched it).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39a02e6b49dc85eb9351bba9f080befa816dda49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/trees/39a02e6b49dc85eb9351bba9f080befa816dda49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/commits/2c9f39cded109f19bdc09ccf8b75ed31b2babb02","verification":{"payload":"tree 39a02e6b49dc85eb9351bba9f080befa816dda49\nparent 48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773\nauthor Jan Jaap <jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790712705 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790712705 +0200\n\nfix(wago): replace resource diagnostics dump with a focused warning card (#1899)\n\nThe WAGO section on the resource overview dumped raw text, listed every\nnode twice and embedded the full controller diagnostics panel.\n\n- Render nothing when the WAGO setup is healthy or the lookup fails.\n- Otherwise show a single HeroUI warning Alert: controller link, one line\n  per affected node (flow editor link) and the concrete conflicting\n  resources, linked.\n- Backend: stop duplicating this resource''s own nodes via the conflict\n  lookup and return conflicting resource ids/names.\n- Drop the dead jest ResourceDiagnostics.spec.tsx (no runner matched it).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvBuBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA76gQAJI27p/GauFv2dKKXmKfiNCb\n2q0kWodjZLVRxmcUAWeWVqC2AvCwNjZ4EebpIIeH/Pj1BIhL4+srG0OsmOgz7r6B\nkRJyC0HCPltsrKZFEGQpdzHE82Kh03/y9WfrZUVw3kUhG/oMdjVbakwcLSpQFDl8\nTD6OLWkAzrBtt6mi06XBUFQMVDicFoBluZU6Fb3LZuomDtW1Jan0u91YC/W+zdfM\nZ1xJtW5IJWyp355CRFaBdpZuBOFFqYClFvPoqYy3DYA4W9JVQ1MEHGQhLnFPenE2\nDZLTeE/Mit+1ALCR+f5spS8bXDg9gZwO/l3lV6RkI7LvfnV76ZQYP5p2fBKwJGGj\nTdzCQdn/s1Jw0n7cz6osSEVrF/glGTChNjQiMRLpAgt/8mOsi9sTuUnuvSEoh0RV\nj0MyO7OWXHM+i36O8OI8EtgtkQ1M4f02pKd7gzWRryzrbwtkZTPFbUvtDs+bgvB1\npD9bT3J4rrSDyDCfVylF/g6oIKakboP92dqo3WuktSB1K8Y/CfWTgTrK0lP7NFqE\n3B2R1/iv13kP/SmNKBYa26o83BVkhPMrS4BHjFdyv2VYarLbsgjykx2kgIx912vF\nDDELialyAaXapisUNaUWZ6Ean9Vte63tTfGYY9y9XutdXcpnIiAKJz7RzsOrEH5w\nlyF7wTHRKfNOeztfaDWh\n=WVOR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T20:11:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/2c9f39cded109f19bdc09ccf8b75ed31b2babb02","node_id":"C_kwDOPIgiztoAKDJjOWYzOWNkZWQxMDlmMTliZGMwOWNjZjhiNzVlZDMxYjJiYWJiMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773","sha":"48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773"}],"sha":"2c9f39cded109f19bdc09ccf8b75ed31b2babb02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/2c9f39cded109f19bdc09ccf8b75ed31b2babb02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10154260?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jappyjan","id":10154260,"login":"jappyjan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTU0MjYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:39:42Z","email":"jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jan Jaap"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:39:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wago): self-heal the RTU bus after a failed read (#1897)\n\nA single RTU timeout or bad frame quarantined the serial bus for the rest of\nthe process lifetime, so a meter glitch left every measurement dead (and\nmetered billing pending) until the runtime was restarted.\n\nAfter a failed read the runtime now waits a quiet period, then re-sends that\nread as a probe and only lifts the quarantine on a fully validated reply;\nfailed probes back off up to 60 s. A failed write still quarantines\npermanently, since it may have reached the device.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2ff396eb8787e33fd006065344b2c2f9f9f75a91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/trees/2ff396eb8787e33fd006065344b2c2f9f9f75a91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/commits/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ff396eb8787e33fd006065344b2c2f9f9f75a91\nparent 85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364\nauthor Jan Jaap <jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790707182 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790707182 +0200\n\nfix(wago): self-heal the RTU bus after a failed read (#1897)\n\nA single RTU timeout or bad frame quarantined the serial bus for the rest of\nthe process lifetime, so a meter glitch left every measurement dead (and\nmetered billing pending) until the runtime was restarted.\n\nAfter a failed read the runtime now waits a quiet period, then re-sends that\nread as a probe and only lifts the quarantine on a fully validated reply;\nfailed probes back off up to 60 s. A failed write still quarantines\npermanently, since it may have reached the device.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvAXuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlD4QAK9tqaqIaAT8kaCFEK2pWYEv\n4vAp16G1sv52+ssFutg4mg9i1jRK19baWXtzOQFkfd3p1hghSvvsj1jb+dzsWEPK\n6Cqaypqfxu9hVyFhqugsZcw/uHGpCNgkQ6iPQ8g4beHS0fgp1IyxbnGqwF73VY1s\nqXavIFWMnCWv8QbLuDG8Fe78fatbigPeAhb23CJ5tRG9r//Qpa/mBIkZzqfGS4Um\nFRHWO/Ct5kxHYdMxEPiDENSwjFiTuzJ/Q08CqJQMjEca2YZ/k5VeUtpV2eeENAJX\nf/dBmZrGOdIao4akugHTIRoBYoagdyATEOYfE+N1WEcjLYPXh50HOBMGV+a4dIjB\nOQsmXcQ0Ykm6t0eDsdXvnW3Agb2XraB7sa5SrtDER3ob6cQJJgAQTOrgaJuSQ5n6\nfpiZaV8oHSl2+YwzV1CWzAyatfg9kdFham0fjb0fvf0hcGrYEKZU5PdhkgVtckTc\n6DCnZvMa/93p5t8U11yqn5Zr0jeo4Z9G6pWBZMu/82tiUuKQteb42hIppKIOvAxw\nO6ZSYvqGW1xp6O+cyfhcXQRLX8Qrb08s5P2jFDIZwNb0a3Ear7UnjtIFQxPpsKxs\ng5en+br5Ntd+moLvcurkQR4h/7m287e3w+ZQh/vYYcmgMJRgYgii2luYZ5p5iWcG\nbDiqw26ZMZe0ktzteHnX\n=0UwF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:39:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773","node_id":"C_kwDOPIgiztoAKDQ4ZGFlZTQ1ZjE3YjJkMWYwNmQ3ODJkYjI3NjVlYWNhMWFlZGI3NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364","sha":"85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364"}],"sha":"48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/48daee45f17b2d1f06d782db2765eaca1aedb773"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289833043?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Giesela-Bot","id":289833043,"login":"Giesela-Bot","node_id":"U_kgDOEUaAUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:38:23Z","email":"mail+giesela@janjaap.de","name":"Giesela-Bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:38:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wago): hide finished commissioning progress, explain runtime updates (#1896)\n\n* fix(wago): hide finished commissioning progress and explain runtime updates (ATT-1102)\n\nEnrollment evidence (permanentConnection + enrollmentRevoked), not the\nbackend''s stuck session.state, now decides when commissioning is \"done\":\nthe controllers table stops offering \"View progress\" once verified, the\ncommissioning modal collapses to a compact read-only summary instead of\nshowing every step/panel at once, and claimed controllers get an explicit\n\"Update runtime\" action that explains today''s only path is a destructive\nre-commission (ATT-1099 will ship the real in-place updater).\n\n* fix(wago): use StandardModal for the runtime-update dialog\n\nMatches the drawer.tsx pattern: plugins can''t import host components\n(module federation shares primitives only), so mirror the host''s\nStandardModal locally with the same bg-overlay contrast fix instead of\ncomposing raw HeroUI Modal primitives.\n\n* feat(plugins-sdk): move StandardModal/StandardDrawer into the plugin SDK\n\nWago''s local modal.tsx (and the pre-existing drawer.tsx elsewhere) mirrored\nhost chrome by hand because module federation only shares @heroui/react\nprimitives, not host components. Move that composition into\nplugins-frontend-sdk so any plugin can import it directly instead of\nre-copying it — placed in the SDK (not plugins-frontend-ui) because that\npackage''s barrel drags in @attraccess/react-query-client via UserSearch,\nwhich isn''t resolvable/appropriate inside a plugin''s self-contained bundle.\n\nThe shared overlay-contrast background is applied as an inline\n`var(--overlay)` style rather than a Tailwind class: each plugin compiles\nits own prefixed Tailwind CSS from its own source, so a class literal in\na shared SDK file would only be picked up by whichever plugin''s build\nhappens to scan it. The CSS custom property itself is global and needs\nno such scanning.\n\nWago''s frontend.standard-modal import needed the SDK''s full barrel\nresolved in both vitest configs and the acceptance-test harness (they\npreviously aliased only the narrower api-client.ts to dodge unrelated\nresolution issues) — widened those aliases and added the matching\ndatabase-entities alias needed by the SDK''s pluggable module.\n\nVerified: full precommit suite (lint/typecheck/build/test for frontend,\napi, generators, plugins-frontend-sdk, plus lint for all plugins) green;\nplugin-wago''s real federation build (nxViteTsPaths, not test aliases)\nbundles cleanly at 320KB with no react-query-client leakage; visual\nre-check via agent-browser against the commissioning-harness fixture in\nlight and dark mode shows identical rendering to the pre-move version.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dea700e57f94024f68f49d3895892450730b4ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/trees/dea700e57f94024f68f49d3895892450730b4ca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/commits/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364","verification":{"payload":"tree dea700e57f94024f68f49d3895892450730b4ca0\nparent b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e\nauthor Giesela-Bot <mail+giesela@janjaap.de> 1790707103 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790707103 +0200\n\nfix(wago): hide finished commissioning progress, explain runtime updates (#1896)\n\n* fix(wago): hide finished commissioning progress and explain runtime updates (ATT-1102)\n\nEnrollment evidence (permanentConnection + enrollmentRevoked), not the\nbackend''s stuck session.state, now decides when commissioning is \"done\":\nthe controllers table stops offering \"View progress\" once verified, the\ncommissioning modal collapses to a compact read-only summary instead of\nshowing every step/panel at once, and claimed controllers get an explicit\n\"Update runtime\" action that explains today''s only path is a destructive\nre-commission (ATT-1099 will ship the real in-place updater).\n\n* fix(wago): use StandardModal for the runtime-update dialog\n\nMatches the drawer.tsx pattern: plugins can''t import host components\n(module federation shares primitives only), so mirror the host''s\nStandardModal locally with the same bg-overlay contrast fix instead of\ncomposing raw HeroUI Modal primitives.\n\n* feat(plugins-sdk): move StandardModal/StandardDrawer into the plugin SDK\n\nWago''s local modal.tsx (and the pre-existing drawer.tsx elsewhere) mirrored\nhost chrome by hand because module federation only shares @heroui/react\nprimitives, not host components. Move that composition into\nplugins-frontend-sdk so any plugin can import it directly instead of\nre-copying it — placed in the SDK (not plugins-frontend-ui) because that\npackage''s barrel drags in @attraccess/react-query-client via UserSearch,\nwhich isn''t resolvable/appropriate inside a plugin''s self-contained bundle.\n\nThe shared overlay-contrast background is applied as an inline\n`var(--overlay)` style rather than a Tailwind class: each plugin compiles\nits own prefixed Tailwind CSS from its own source, so a class literal in\na shared SDK file would only be picked up by whichever plugin''s build\nhappens to scan it. The CSS custom property itself is global and needs\nno such scanning.\n\nWago''s frontend.standard-modal import needed the SDK''s full barrel\nresolved in both vitest configs and the acceptance-test harness (they\npreviously aliased only the narrower api-client.ts to dodge unrelated\nresolution issues) — widened those aliases and added the matching\ndatabase-entities alias needed by the SDK''s pluggable module.\n\nVerified: full precommit suite (lint/typecheck/build/test for frontend,\napi, generators, plugins-frontend-sdk, plus lint for all plugins) green;\nplugin-wago''s real federation build (nxViteTsPaths, not test aliases)\nbundles cleanly at 320KB with no react-query-client leakage; visual\nre-check via agent-browser against the commissioning-harness fixture in\nlight and dark mode shows identical rendering to the pre-move version.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvAWfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0DEQAHb7Omk0ZB4Alil72T/tXgc2\ntnbUWMcxDopyx4cUAEXxvJ1vWcJR5WLMtxZel7+WAclWT+Yo+Bekb+BuXDYiGAeA\nK7zfjVvNx53RdFy3dXtUQKlDycgk+hnTOX5+4p3e57xjK0KT52Xqe4T6EtCWH+1W\nxS5FfEpLFle1/SCYAJ2IHEtdY3C7cIkODUXXHxFdknnaTHKAr7A0AS1z8k1s0lye\nt8a4eBUOnyvWnBM3BXsI3nOw0IIP9fryaDE/ZE4YcvekEOdYmDQ2j0tBjXNS2vEa\nX5omgxs3ww8TiZDx1+Rbq90e892OkVxk/ePt2PsG/1VO6qfHW8Wt4AJkEqIkuEuC\nD3wI4jGGtteCxAs9CU/+hhKu7Izf30K/FcJXfe4NCLem6+z7kfaQljaEsjg7LnPR\nlp7Vb57AlIsPSqZuzWUrPhIeawvdG1akBokZKtDWGGKkrhYMA8KDCpgntLPUgPfS\niSUr9p0AleDAAIrpdbLwKHHN/3+G9uh4VYssq82zePJRogJi2UWa5RGxwwrZq5pe\nrydwYIkZ5qvsWjyeOg3u5YkND2dabXQRASyPL6tPKtg5IgHhZy3ifPPPssKt+5qc\nFCNzShV2OxPL6xM1vecNLbUiqACXYTiV+d9T3hMXOk/P26vEmWkdQ1AAIiKQ43wI\ngEbPGZjQOQZPhnjrJzFT\n=kzQX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:38:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364","node_id":"C_kwDOPIgiztoAKDg1ZGU0ZTM2ODU0NTVjMzJiOWJhMWVhOTQ1OTc0Mjg5MDE2ZmIzNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e","sha":"b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e"}],"sha":"85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/85de4e3685455c32b9ba1ea945974289016fb364"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289833043?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Giesela-Bot","id":289833043,"login":"Giesela-Bot","node_id":"U_kgDOEUaAUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giesela-Bot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:38:54Z","email":"mail+giesela@janjaap.de","name":"Giesela-Bot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:38:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(billing): flow-defined energy meters with automatic per-kWh billing (ATT-1101) (#1895)\n\n* feat(billing): add flow-defined energy meters with automatic per-kWh billing\n\nA resource can bill energy per kWh through a meter defined by dedicated flow\nbranches (metering start/ready, metering collection/report). Attraccess\ninitializes the meter before start effects, collects a fresh final total after\nstop effects, and adds an exact, auditable ENERGY line item. Unavailable data\nleaves the energy charge pending with retry/waive instead of billing zero.\nIncludes live meter values and cost in the resource overview.\n\n* fix(billing): bill late energy as a correction transaction and clarify pending-energy card\n\nA retried energy settlement no longer mutates the completed usage bill; it\ncreates a separate correction transaction (correctionOfId) so bills stay\nimmutable. The pending/failed energy card now explains what happened and what\neach action does.\n\n* feat(billing): audit and live-notify energy correction transactions\n\nCorrection transactions from a retried energy settlement are now written to\nthe billing audit log (source energy-correction, after commit) and pushed to\nthe user''s live transaction stream like every other billing transaction.\n\n* fix(billing): address energy metering review findings\n\n- fail closed when a configured baseline/observed-at template renders empty\n- mark the outgoing meter compromised only when a takeover start fails, and fail (not retry) such sessions\n- throttle interim polling by last attempt and skip sessions with an interim run in flight\n- surface meter failure reasons in the frontend toast and add METER_SESSION_NOT_FOUND\n- localize the ENERGY receipt line item in the email template\n- give correctionOfId a cascading foreign key and export it in the billing CSV\n- audit waived energy charges with the acting user\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f679918b720fbcd60b5ab290d09407cdaecd64cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/trees/f679918b720fbcd60b5ab290d09407cdaecd64cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/commits/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e","verification":{"payload":"tree f679918b720fbcd60b5ab290d09407cdaecd64cb\nparent 0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21\nauthor Giesela-Bot <mail+giesela@janjaap.de> 1790678334 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790678334 +0200\n\nfeat(billing): flow-defined energy meters with automatic per-kWh billing (ATT-1101) (#1895)\n\n* feat(billing): add flow-defined energy meters with automatic per-kWh billing\n\nA resource can bill energy per kWh through a meter defined by dedicated flow\nbranches (metering start/ready, metering collection/report). Attraccess\ninitializes the meter before start effects, collects a fresh final total after\nstop effects, and adds an exact, auditable ENERGY line item. Unavailable data\nleaves the energy charge pending with retry/waive instead of billing zero.\nIncludes live meter values and cost in the resource overview.\n\n* fix(billing): bill late energy as a correction transaction and clarify pending-energy card\n\nA retried energy settlement no longer mutates the completed usage bill; it\ncreates a separate correction transaction (correctionOfId) so bills stay\nimmutable. The pending/failed energy card now explains what happened and what\neach action does.\n\n* feat(billing): audit and live-notify energy correction transactions\n\nCorrection transactions from a retried energy settlement are now written to\nthe billing audit log (source energy-correction, after commit) and pushed to\nthe user''s live transaction stream like every other billing transaction.\n\n* fix(billing): address energy metering review findings\n\n- fail closed when a configured baseline/observed-at template renders empty\n- mark the outgoing meter compromised only when a takeover start fails, and fail (not retry) such sessions\n- throttle interim polling by last attempt and skip sessions with an interim run in flight\n- surface meter failure reasons in the frontend toast and add METER_SESSION_NOT_FOUND\n- localize the ENERGY receipt line item in the email template\n- give correctionOfId a cascading foreign key and export it in the billing CSV\n- audit waived energy charges with the acting user\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu5U+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6c4QAE5xW+tCQajnyAbvSovaXKaC\nYZPx7Gs1Lvfr3HTwYc9tovI4R2KtFWhEMvP3ZqHqz64oCA/7tMBFKpzLcLY6GeRT\nBvZbHGm0Cbznd9y98b9rOmggY5YSIrmX5LV+ammTAkkr2s3HNfyJf3lE6xpKXoVj\np7JI5MGna13THoUb3rtt9Utk2hvNlyYdaFAFaH6mMcfVmqUadBpIvVtqOSqDCa1/\nkboHiVnx2UDBPCWkkxzwlLB7m4x7Ml7GXopoUnYIWjzSukPY5zTea+h1ZOHJ7IjD\nhBhbG9cQY5Ng3UKKFxcRtypXM3IqBFOreGLjKb5bZi69VURztNLJ+HZXTKP0JgvW\nGfN5S7hk4LNxnPZngmuD8OPRpeSHYYzwsxL+8kBVCauK3J5EdlWI9K/XqgNuOpL8\nzSNagz15yuX7PKcZXpHyNsQtsFhNAgRTAvJbb0zuZhd28BpLp+6BVuLJ+P1djhm2\nHEbmNXeWnyFz4PKIAoFZ++amzN37rlM8+v6OvccftvjDkSBx0BEq/7cyf0mBGEJ+\nUjvSvkVU/gyCQ5g/dabApxPUO3Cp8FdBezVi/2CCzFfE5bfJS9XHjGpCzhwXnez5\nZWzGu72lGm2ilpUQ+bI3x9qcabWL0QS66qbf6Asv3QcaoPzd5+om/aRIOidpdaeR\nszeMAtHgFWUdaQSNQQVU\n=bDcA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T10:38:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e","node_id":"C_kwDOPIgiztoAKGI3NmRhNDk4M2I1MzM4MWVmOWVhZjBjODYxNWVjZTc5ZDRhOWNhNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Attraccess/Attraccess/commit/0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21","sha":"0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21"}],"sha":"b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/b76da4983b53381ef9eaf0c8615ece79d4a9ca6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10154260?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jappyjan","id":10154260,"login":"jappyjan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTU0MjYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jappyjan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/commits/0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:17:08Z","email":"jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jan Jaap"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T20:17:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wago): recover plugin loading and simplify commissioning (#1881)\n\n* fix(plugins): recover WAGO startup and frontend loading\n\n* fix(plugins): replace refreshed instances and validate WAGO prefix\n\n* fix(wago): simplify CC100 commissioning and report storage errors\n\n* test(wago): make plugin-wago specs deterministic against migration order and CI timing\n\n- claim-intent-migration: the lease-drop migration added a final registry\n  entry, so the guarded claim-intent downgrade is now the fourth undo,\n  not the third.\n- visual-editor: pause the 5 s diagnostics refetchInterval during the\n  exact-count window. react-query''s interval tick only refetches while\n  focusManager.isFocused(), which reads document.visibilityState at tick\n  time; a slow runner could otherwise interleave a background poll with\n  the manual refresh and observe two calls.\n\n* feat(wago): CC100 Modbus RTU, unsigned releases, clock skew tolerance and RUN LED status (#1894)\n\n* fix(wago): tolerate 5 s positive controller clock skew\n\nTelemetry, flow reads/waits, runtime readiness and heartbeat-gated credential\nrotation rejected controller timestamps even 1 ms ahead of the server. Share\nthe commissioning clock tolerance (5 s) via shared/clock.ts. Source times are\nkept; stale-age, sequence and replay checks are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* perf(wago): skip kernel-typed descriptors in the host IO guard\n\nSockets, pipes, directories and devices cannot alias the regular sysfs DOUT\nfile. Skipping them with shell builtins avoids spawning BusyBox stat parsers\nper descriptor, which exhausted the FW31 live gate deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): CC100 RS-485 Modbus RTU profile for the WAGO 879-3000 meter\n\nAdd the cc100-751-9301-fw31-digital-rtu-v1 hardware profile: the installer\nverifies the FW31 RS-485 UART and dialout group and passes only /dev/ttySTM1\nas /dev/serial; the runtime routes RTU Modbus devices through it and rejects\nother serial paths. Add the documented 879-3000 register map with optional\nper-measurement rounding, 9600 8N1 defaults and the matching editor controls.\n\nThe installer also waits (bounded) for a busy controller lock and gives the\nslow FW31 image import its own 300 s budget; acceptance requires the runtime\nto be enabled and running.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): unsigned compressed runtime releases resolved at delivery\n\nDrop release signatures: bundles are a gzip-compressed image in the outer tar\nplus a SHA-256 checksum, which fits FW31 staging storage (82 MB vs 236 MB).\nThe importer, catalog, packager, CI workflow and acceptance fixtures take the\ntwo-file release.\n\nSessions no longer pin a release: each delivery attempt resolves the current\ncatalog release and rechecks it before transfer, so retries and legacy\nsessions install the current build. A busy controller lock now surfaces as a\nretryable error without leaving a phantom recovery token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): show verified enrollment state in commissioning UI\n\nShare a useCommissioningVerification hook between the commissioning modal and\nthe controllers table. Enrollment is shown as complete once permanent MQTT\naccess and enrollment revocation are verified, separately from pending\nconfiguration, hardware probe and management hardening. Drop the pinned\nrelease display and request field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): show CC100 runtime health on the RUN LED\n\nThe runtime drives the RUN LED dies (green, red, both = yellow) from its\nreadiness: steady yellow while starting, yellow blink while pairing, red blink\nwhen the broker is unreachable, green/yellow while unconfigured, mostly red on\nfaults, and a green heartbeat with a periodic light show when ready.\n\nThe installer grants UID 10001 write access to the two brightness files on\nevery boot and bind-mounts them only when present. The LED is cosmetic: a\nmissing mount or permission disables it without affecting I/O. WAGO ledserverd\nkeeps RUN at STATIC_OFF once CODESYS is disabled, so it does not compete.\nVerified on a FW31 751-9301 bench unit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* test(wago): align specs with delivery release checks and durable enablement\n\n- claim-intent-migration: the drop-wago-commissioning-lease migration added a\n  final registry entry, so the guarded claim-intent downgrade is now the\n  fourth undo, not the third.\n- runtime-lifecycle-interruption: a rejected boot keeps runtime-enabled\n  (durable operator intent), and the interrupted acceptance snapshots\n  docker.log after its new read-only running inspect.\n- audit-hooks integration: mock WagoRuntimeArtifactsService.current() to the\n  acquired release so assertCurrentRuntimeBundle passes during delivery.\n\n* test(wago): pause diagnostics refetchInterval during the exact-count window\n\nThe diagnostics query polls every 5 s in real time. On a loaded CI runner\nthe mount-to-assert span can cross an interval boundary, so a background\npoll landed between mockClear and the manual refresh and\ntoHaveBeenCalledTimes(1) observed two calls. Mark the document hidden for\nthe measured window: react-query''s interval tick only refetches while\nfocusManager.isFocused(), which reads document.visibilityState at tick\ntime, while the explicit refresh click is unaffected.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): version plugin bundle URLs and harden npm discovery\n\n- Tag federation remote and stylesheet URLs with the plugin version so a\n  version bump is not served from the browser''s module cache.\n- Keep npm-* directories discoverable when the npm state file is unreadable.\n- Reserve the npm-* namespace so ZIP uploads cannot be silently dropped.\n- Retry fixture directory removal to stop ENOTEMPTY flakes in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"abdb7c29b28d7019c50310df76a0996bb0285f0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/trees/abdb7c29b28d7019c50310df76a0996bb0285f0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Attraccess/Attraccess/git/commits/0f6c40724504a966edb1ef127c8068193a058d21","verification":{"payload":"tree abdb7c29b28d7019c50310df76a0996bb0285f0a\nparent afa58e8a5eadfb340f317e6ec3227af0cf9b6c54\nauthor Jan Jaap <jappyjan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790626628 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790626628 +0200\n\nfix(wago): recover plugin loading and simplify commissioning (#1881)\n\n* fix(plugins): recover WAGO startup and frontend loading\n\n* fix(plugins): replace refreshed instances and validate WAGO prefix\n\n* fix(wago): simplify CC100 commissioning and report storage errors\n\n* test(wago): make plugin-wago specs deterministic against migration order and CI timing\n\n- claim-intent-migration: the lease-drop migration added a final registry\n  entry, so the guarded claim-intent downgrade is now the fourth undo,\n  not the third.\n- visual-editor: pause the 5 s diagnostics refetchInterval during the\n  exact-count window. react-query''s interval tick only refetches while\n  focusManager.isFocused(), which reads document.visibilityState at tick\n  time; a slow runner could otherwise interleave a background poll with\n  the manual refresh and observe two calls.\n\n* feat(wago): CC100 Modbus RTU, unsigned releases, clock skew tolerance and RUN LED status (#1894)\n\n* fix(wago): tolerate 5 s positive controller clock skew\n\nTelemetry, flow reads/waits, runtime readiness and heartbeat-gated credential\nrotation rejected controller timestamps even 1 ms ahead of the server. Share\nthe commissioning clock tolerance (5 s) via shared/clock.ts. Source times are\nkept; stale-age, sequence and replay checks are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* perf(wago): skip kernel-typed descriptors in the host IO guard\n\nSockets, pipes, directories and devices cannot alias the regular sysfs DOUT\nfile. Skipping them with shell builtins avoids spawning BusyBox stat parsers\nper descriptor, which exhausted the FW31 live gate deadline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): CC100 RS-485 Modbus RTU profile for the WAGO 879-3000 meter\n\nAdd the cc100-751-9301-fw31-digital-rtu-v1 hardware profile: the installer\nverifies the FW31 RS-485 UART and dialout group and passes only /dev/ttySTM1\nas /dev/serial; the runtime routes RTU Modbus devices through it and rejects\nother serial paths. Add the documented 879-3000 register map with optional\nper-measurement rounding, 9600 8N1 defaults and the matching editor controls.\n\nThe installer also waits (bounded) for a busy controller lock and gives the\nslow FW31 image import its own 300 s budget; acceptance requires the runtime\nto be enabled and running.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): unsigned compressed runtime releases resolved at delivery\n\nDrop release signatures: bundles are a gzip-compressed image in the outer tar\nplus a SHA-256 checksum, which fits FW31 staging storage (82 MB vs 236 MB).\nThe importer, catalog, packager, CI workflow and acceptance fixtures take the\ntwo-file release.\n\nSessions no longer pin a release: each delivery attempt resolves the current\ncatalog release and rechecks it before transfer, so retries and legacy\nsessions install the current build. A busy controller lock now surfaces as a\nretryable error without leaving a phantom recovery token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): show verified enrollment state in commissioning UI\n\nShare a useCommissioningVerification hook between the commissioning modal and\nthe controllers table. Enrollment is shown as complete once permanent MQTT\naccess and enrollment revocation are verified, separately from pending\nconfiguration, hardware probe and management hardening. Drop the pinned\nrelease display and request field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* feat(wago): show CC100 runtime health on the RUN LED\n\nThe runtime drives the RUN LED dies (green, red, both = yellow) from its\nreadiness: steady yellow while starting, yellow blink while pairing, red blink\nwhen the broker is unreachable, green/yellow while unconfigured, mostly red on\nfaults, and a green heartbeat with a periodic light show when ready.\n\nThe installer grants UID 10001 write access to the two brightness files on\nevery boot and bind-mounts them only when present. The LED is cosmetic: a\nmissing mount or permission disables it without affecting I/O. WAGO ledserverd\nkeeps RUN at STATIC_OFF once CODESYS is disabled, so it does not compete.\nVerified on a FW31 751-9301 bench unit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QbfJzS9K8n5AQ3MsXj71X9\n\n* test(wago): align specs with delivery release checks and durable enablement\n\n- claim-intent-migration: the drop-wago-commissioning-lease migration added a\n  final registry entry, so the guarded claim-intent downgrade is now the\n  fourth undo, not the third.\n- runtime-lifecycle-interruption: a rejected boot keeps runtime-enabled\n  (durable operator intent), and the interrupted acceptance snapshots\n  docker.log after its new read-only running inspect.\n- audit-hooks integration: mock WagoRuntimeArtifactsService.current() to the\n  acquired release so assertCurrentRuntimeBundle passes during delivery.\n\n* test(wago): pause diagnostics refetchInterval during the exact-count window\n\nThe diagnostics query polls every 5 s in real time. On a loaded CI runner\nthe mount-to-assert span can cross an interval boundary, so a background\npoll landed between mockClear and the manual refresh and\ntoHaveBeenCalledTimes(1) observed two calls. Mark the document hidden for\nthe measured window: react-query''s interval tick only refetches while\nfocusManager.isFocused(), which reads document.visibilityState at tick\ntime, while the explicit refresh click is unaffected.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): version plugin bundle URLs and harden npm discovery\n\n- Tag federation remote and stylesheet URLs with the plugin version so a\n  version bump is not served from the browser''s module cache.\n- Keep npm-* directories discoverable when the npm state file is unreadable.\n- Reserve the npm-* namespace so ZIP uploads cannot be silently dropped.\n- Retry fixture directory removal to stop ENOTEMPTY flakes in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Giesela-Bot <289833043+Giesela-Bot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqustECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA1AQAHcIzvskR1NhXqCgC5xI1FPs\njY+zkVqK0WPiVvrWFWUXEDCrc6x0KLCV8yRpyvOa1shxfnXh5D/lT+LPn+mJ5a0r\nKFACyq3WiQCMqw+dpGZ5jn5BvvfjB5b/X9rnY+YqxqskvtiE2f38NV6LCekmrSOB\nEFnYvRc0JpzXLf5wIjUxpZyP+gnqCZW4+yci8g4w0Z/2Uj/vGsVxz8mGK36sCokL\nTULd2MSAlgO95JyPc/n+6P/trdt4tXozwuGjpGWda/hUgJQmE5QcPEjy8UeFhq0/\nCc3Dr8UjclDpZs083cfh4kfE3W+FtsVdVaqxwQbDVRFLFMWSBasYe6vofEzEg1fc\n8udFAZsw+SBMKqgladSsmCeWp126osv0+NFmrDqaON9wQH0CfmHk34jJBNV8coAx\nNPLNmdBk4DYbxjKuo1deAkxcy/qJaNBolbBJH2Cz5MTww0fZXTj8voIxGpLnUyeW\nGqWoDKMwQKUmAT0ms05gFdBh5ubm0BWIPbGq9LL+I77pNxMIS/gFguUYcICp14QA\ncZkL2PFrWSlzffO/dN9pr5skPJUJ/h8Yxfb1C1skAYc7bHEfatnaurJgsPXUy8bU\nKryxv7gV5jmN01DPPqNFitdtxQ8MnvFhhQdXBzoEUZ7yA6RnNWGgrfKC9KulXIi8\n699Io+gsnIaeCpJieF7W\n=zkwS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T20:17:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.